  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of a monatomic ideal gas undergoes the cyclic process $\\mathrm{J} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{K} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{L} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{J}$, as shown in the P-T diagram.\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0003_356e25d57edd.png\">\nMatch the quantities mentioned in List-I with their values in List-II and choose the correct option.\n[$\\mathcal{R}$ is the gas constant.]\r\n\\(\\begin{array}{l|l}\r\n\\text{List-I} & \\text{List-II} \\\\\r\n\\hline \\text{(P) Work done in the complete cyclic process} & (1) \\mathcal{R} T_0-4 \\mathcal{R} T_0 \\ln 2 \\\\\r\n\\text{(Q) Change in the internal energy of the gas in the process JK} & (2) 0 \\\\\r\n\\text{(R) Heat given to the gas in the process KL} & (3) 3 \\mathcal{R} T_0 \\\\\r\n\\text{(S) Change in the internal energy of the gas in the process MJ} & (4) -2 \\mathcal{R} T_0 \\ln 2 \\\\\r\n& (5) -3 \\mathcal{R} T_0 \\ln 2\r\n\\end{array}\\)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 1 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 3 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 5 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 4 ; \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 3 ; \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 5 ; \\mathrm{S} \\rightarrow 2$",
